error[E0277]: `BTreeMap<std::string::String, u64>` cannot be flattened into another object
  --> tests/ui/macros/schema_tagged_newtype_map.rs:10:13
   |
10 |     Counted(BTreeMap<String, u64>),
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ does not name its members
   |
   = help: the trait `kynos::schema::Flatten` is not implemented for `BTreeMap<std::string::String, u64>`
   = note: a flattened field's members become the parent's own, so its schema has to name them; a map names none, so its values would reach the properties the object declared itself
   = note: give it a named field of its own, or, on a `HashMap` or `BTreeMap` field, add `#[schema(open)]` beside `#[serde(flatten)]` to say the object really is open -- the values then become the object's `unevaluatedProperties`
